\f0\b\fs36 \cf6 \strokec6 Readings\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 The material covered in the course will be available in the presentation slides which will be fairly self-contained. The slides will be made available via Canvas.\
Optional text-book readings include\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://szeliski.org/Book/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Computer Vision: Algorithms and Applications}}, by\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://szeliski.org/RichardSzeliski.htm"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Richard Szeliski}}. An online version is available, or you may purchase the book at a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.springer.com/computer/image+processing/book/978-1-84882-934-3"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 variety}}\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.amazon.com/Computer-Vision-Algorithms-Applications-Science/dp/1848829345/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 of}}\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://search.barnesandnoble.com/Computer-Vision/Richard-Szeliski/e/9781848829343/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 locations}}. Also see Robot Vision by Berthold KP Horn and Optics by E. Hecht.\
\
